# COVERAGE FIXTURE. Deliberate test data, not an ontology about anything.
#
# RULE: scm-svf2
# W3C OWL 2 Web Ontology Language Profiles (Second Edition), section 4.3,
# Table 9: The Semantics of Schema Vocabulary.
# https://www.w3.org/TR/owl2-profiles/#Reasoning_in_OWL_2_RL_and_RDF_Graphs_using_Rules
#
#   T(?c1, owl:someValuesFrom, ?y)
#   T(?c1, owl:onProperty, ?p1)
#   T(?c2, owl:someValuesFrom, ?y)
#   T(?c2, owl:onProperty, ?p2)
#   T(?p1, rdfs:subPropertyOf, ?p2)
#     ->  T(?c1, rdfs:subClassOf, ?c2)
#
# WHY IT EXISTS. scm-svf2 needs two someValuesFrom restrictions over the SAME
# filler whose properties are related by rdfs:subPropertyOf. Nothing in this
# repository has that shape, so tools/horn_differential.py compared the Rust and
# Python engines on scm-svf2 zero times and its clean sweep said nothing about
# it. Its sibling scm-svf1, which needs one shared property and two fillers
# related by rdfs:subClassOf, does fire in the corpus; the two differ only in
# WHICH of the two positions carries the ordering, which is exactly the kind of
# difference a reader assumes is covered because the neighbour is.
#
# EXPECTED: exactly one derivation, credited to scm-svf2:
#   :R1 rdfs:subClassOf :R2
#
# scm-svf1 does not also fire: it would need :C rdfs:subClassOf :C, which this
# file does not assert, and the built-in table has no reflexivity rule.

@prefix : <http://ex.org/cover/scm-svf2#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

:R1 a owl:Restriction ;
    owl:onProperty :p1 ;
    owl:someValuesFrom :C .

:R2 a owl:Restriction ;
    owl:onProperty :p2 ;
    owl:someValuesFrom :C .

:p1 rdfs:subPropertyOf :p2 .
